<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
     R-1106 (register; technical-design §12.4, NFR-6a, FR-PLT-5, FR-STO-8, constitution V): the
     manifest already sets `android:allowBackup="false"`, which on its own already refuses both
     cloud backup and Android's device-to-device (D2D) "Switch"/restore transfer for this app on
     every API level — but the technical design calls for *both* `allowBackup="false"` **and** an
     explicit `data_extraction_rules` exclusion, and leaving the second half undeclared is exactly
     what R-1106 found: an app whose first principle is that audio and its content stay on the
     device should say so explicitly, in the one place API 31+'s own backup/transfer framework
     reads, rather than relying on a single flag nobody has to re-read to trust. This file is
     therefore belt-and-suspenders by design, not a second independent guarantee — if
     `allowBackup` were ever flipped to `true` by mistake, this file is what would still stop a
     cloud backup or a device transfer from carrying anything.

     Every category the constitution and functional spec name is covered by excluding the whole
     app sandbox, deliberately, rather than picked apart field by field:
       - captured/retained audio (constitution V, FR-PLT-5, FR-STO-8/AC-81 — audio is app-private,
         never exposed to the system media store, so it lives only under this domain)
       - the Room database (transmissions, transcripts, attributions, corrections, threads,
         stations, superseded-transcript history)
       - user-supplied station names and any station knowledge (FR-DIG-13 — never leaves the
         device in any channel; a stray backup is exactly such a leave)
       - voiceprints and embeddings (FR-SPK-20 — the *only* declared exception for these is the
         operator-invoked, in-app export/restore bundle (FR-STO-6, `:data`'s
         `BackupRestoreCoordinator`), which the operator triggers and which states what it carries;
         that is a different, already-declared channel from the OS's own backup/transfer, which
         must carry none of this by default)
       - any token, credential or analytics queue held in shared preferences or a keystore-backed
         file

     `domain="root"` covers the app's entire private storage tree (files, databases, shared
     preferences) in one exclusion. No `external`, `device_protected` or `media` domain is
     declared because this app never writes there in the first place (FR-STO-8/AC-81); adding an
     exclusion for a domain nothing is ever written to would document a false capability rather
     than a true guarantee, so the exclusion list matches what the app actually does, not merely
     what would be safe to also list.

     Excluding *everything* is deliberate, not merely the default: this app has nothing in its own
     storage that is meant to leave the device by this route. The four declared outbound
     channels (constitution V) — user-initiated export/share, corpus contribution, the field
     report, and analytics — are each their own explicit, operator-visible, closed-field path with
     its own consent and its own payload construction; none of them is "restore my phone onto a
     new one" or "back this app up to my cloud account", which is what this file governs instead.
-->
<data-extraction-rules>
    <cloud-backup>
        <exclude domain="root" />
    </cloud-backup>
    <device-transfer>
        <exclude domain="root" />
    </device-transfer>
</data-extraction-rules>
